You can use PHP's DOMDocument class to parse the HTML and extract the specific content you want. Here's an example:

```
$pageContent = file_get_contents('http://www.pullcontentshere.com/');
$doc = new DOMDocument();
$doc->loadHTML($pageContent);
$div = $doc->getElementById('myContent');
$content = $doc->saveHTML($div);
echo $content;
```

First, we load the page content into a DOMDocument object. Then, we use the `getElementById` method to select the `<div>` element we want (with the ID "myContent"). Finally, we use the `saveHTML` method to extract the HTML content of that element and save it to the `$content` variable.

Note: make sure to use `loadHTML` instead of `loadHTMLFile`, as file_get_contents returns a string, not a file.
